Workstream ID: forward-deployed-engineering
Title: Research-backed Forward Deployed Engineering background mission
Status: IN_REVIEW
Milestone: Add an evidence-based customer-to-production engineering roadmap
Dependencies: tracker-foundation, versioned-roadmaps, career-graph, encrypted-progress-journal, discovery-atlas
GitHub issue: https://github.com/Zanark/CareerOS/issues/10
Purpose: Add a deeply researched Forward Deployed Engineering mission in the
  background, integrated with every applicable mission surface. Preserve existing
  progress, focus choices, frozen curricula and the complete Discovery Atlas.

Tasks:
  [x] Review primary employer roles and technical/customer-delivery sources.
  [x] Trace mission identity, stored state, journal replay, learning and graph boundaries.
  [x] Author a progressive, cited curriculum with meaningful artifacts and diagnostics.
  [x] Add background defaults and strictly compatible old-workspace normalization.
  [x] Integrate mission views, roadmap/library/search, colors and graph relationships.
  [x] Support evidence, planning, recall, activity and source-derived Atlas recognition.
  [x] Preserve backups, encrypted append/replay and tutorial isolation.
  [x] Update focused research/source/usage/architecture references and tutorial.
  [x] Qualify domain, compatibility and actual responsive browser workflows.
  [x] Keep a separate live development preview available for user monitoring.
  [ ] Publish authorized source and verify exact successful Pages artifacts/live behavior.
  [ ] Settle this issue, original Kanban item, evidence and owned continuity.

Acceptance criteria:
  The new mission is background and unstarted on new and compatible old workspaces;
    no existing primary mission, modes, checkpoint, evidence or dates are rewritten.
  The roadmap covers discovery, engineering/data/integration, responsible AI,
    production operations, adoption, handoff, product feedback and interview proof.
  Author-created sequence and criteria are distinguished from employer requirements.
  Sources expose reviewed scope, vendor-specific assumptions and unstable job listings.
  No paid account, real customer data or unsupervised production access is mandatory.
  All existing mission-supporting views recognize the new stable identity.
  The graph explains real cross-mission transfer without granting equivalent credit.
  Atlas remains the same finite collection, deriving recognition from FDE evidence
    and eligible recall; no separate score, reset or fabricated professional rank.
  Old schema-one/two backups and encrypted journal chains retain actual records.
  Invalid FDE data fails explicitly; missing old data is not treated as corruption.
  Technical completion, human acceptance and exact-source publication stay separate.

Completion evidence:
  Primary employer descriptions reviewed include Palantir, OpenAI, Anthropic,
    Baseten and Modal; specialist expectations differ and are not universal gates.
  docs/FDE-RESEARCH.md records five research lenses and all 24 source review scopes.
  Original design: 48 core checkpoints, 8 optional units, 112 applied/transfer exercises;
    13 curated comparisons touch all 9 old missions. Native FDE recall/Atlas retain
    the existing completion/retention/discovery semantics, not a new career score.
  Latest observed complete type/unit gate: 702 PASS; tracking cases: 22 PASS.
  Genuine old 9-mission encrypted baseline/old-batch replay followed by new FDE append
    passes; explicit mission deletion rejects. Frozen source editions stay intact.
  All 8 new FDE native browser cases pass within the broader affected gate.
  Affected gate: 108 of 109 passed initially; the only failure was the old
    six-more-active-missions expectation, now seven. Its focused rerun passes.
  Complete 177-step tutorial passes at 1440, 390 and 320 pixels. Existing graph
    spacing, source workbooks, themes, maps, Atlas and old-record flows are covered.
  Earlier singular/plural discovery expectation was corrected without a runtime
    change; exactly one new discovery correctly uses the singular notice.
  Three actual responsive/theme lesson captures reviewed without clipping seen.
  User preview serves current source with live updates on loopback port 4468;
    HTTP and actual Fieldcraft rendering verified in a disposable browser.
  Source publication, full hosted gate and exact live-artifact verification remain
    pending. No human acceptance or user progress access is claimed.

